    <data key="d0" xml:space="preserve"/>
    <node id="n0">
      <data key="d6">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry height="747.6" width="1150.0" x="200.0" y="0.0"/>
          <y:Fill hasColor="false" transparent="false"/>
          <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="left" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Consolas" fontSize="14" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="606.0" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="1081.6171875" x="34.19140625" xml:space="preserve" y="10.0">G:two-way-walk-5x5:

   x12345
  y#######    B - beginning cell (1,3), Agent starts here facing right (towards x = 5) and need to reach one of end cells.
  1##### #    E - upper end cell (5,1).
  2##### #    E - lower end cell (5,5).
  3#     #
  4##### #
  5##### #
   #######

Agent will got:
 1. Small penalty for each move (except for pass move), so need to find shortest way.
 2. Prize for reaching any of the end cells.

There is 2 ways, both of the same length, so both cost the same:
  1. (1,3)-&gt;(2,3)-&gt;(3,3)-&gt;(4,3)-&gt;(5,3)-&gt;(5,2)-&gt;(5,1):
     Agent rotates left in the cell (5,3) and walks up to the upper end cell.
  2. (1,3)-&gt;(2,3)-&gt;(3,3)-&gt;(4,3)-&gt;(5,3)-&gt;(5,4)-&gt;(5,5):
     Agent rotates right in the cell (5,3) and walks down to the lower end cell.

Map variables:
  Agent observe the number of the cell he currently in. Agent can move forward (step into the cell in front
of him), rotate left and right, also do nothing.

Input hidden variables:
  cell number: 'C', {&lt;number in format (x,y)&gt;}

Output hidden variables:
  action: 'A', {'f' - forward, 'l' - rotate left, 'r' - rotate right, 'p' - pass (do nothing)}

Label formats:
  Graph label: 'G:&lt;graph name&gt;:&lt;optional description&gt;', example: 'G:Pacman 5x3:this description'
  IO variable label: '&lt;I or O&gt;:&lt;name&gt;:&lt;bool or int or float or list&gt;:&lt;range&gt;:&lt;optional description&gt;', example: 'I:C:list:cell number'
  Hidden concrete value label: 'C:&lt;in/out variable name&gt;:&lt;value&gt;:&lt;node name&gt;:&lt;optional description&gt;', example: 'C:A:f:n1:step in cell (2,3)'
  Hidden abstract value label: 'A:&lt;node name&gt;:&lt;optional description&gt;', example: 'A:n2:step in cell (2,3)'
  Sample label: 'S:&lt;sample id/name&gt;:&lt;probability count&gt;:&lt;utility&gt;:&lt;optional description&gt;', eample: 'S:S1:123:-5.5:hit the wall'

Variable range:
  bool: &lt;t;f&gt;, example: 'I:O:bool:t;f:true or false or unobserved variable',  'I:O:bool:t:true or unobserved variable'
  int:  &lt;min;max&gt;, example: 'I:O:int:1;10:integer from 1 to 10 or unobserved variable'
  float: &lt;min;max&gt;, example: 'I:O:float:0.0;1.0:float from 0.0 to 1.0 or unobserved variable'
  list: &lt;list of possible values separated by ;&gt;, example: 'I:O:list:a;b;1;2:list of possible values or unobserved variable'<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="-0.5" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="-0.5" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="10.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="roundrectangle"/>
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
